omains to be activated by Arisen. Super cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:03:37-07:00","id":1067196,"title":"","content":"What's happening in it? I've not got time to read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:48:00-07:00","id":1067216,"title":"","content":"The Mutupos (the local Orders) are interesting in that they seem to reinforce the idea that the Orders are social roles first rather that philosophies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:21:40-07:00","id":1067250,"title":"","content":"So far, this has been my favorite chapter in the Dark Eras Companion. I am curious about what Path and Order Tools the Shona would use. High Speech is referenced as is using Pillar points to create powerful Yantras for the subtle arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T22:12:18-07:00","id":1067407,"title":"","content":"To me, it's funny they call Mana by way of Simba. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I know it comes from 90s movie association, but I cannot resist...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgflip.com/1lzwvt.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> On the other hand, I'm a bit shocked that Portuguese use term Vis for this energy - I always assumed Mana was used by Christdom mages from the old spelling of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manna\" target=\"_blank\">Old Testament Manna</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T00:16:21-07:00","id":1067432,"title":"","content":"Well in general I rather liked this Era write-up ( still I think there is too much source on native mediums - sssoooo many terms to use and be confused in game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), I'm <i>really</i> disappointed we do not see more than paragraph on relations between Mutapa and Atlantean mages. I really wanted to read how Diamond Orders are coming and making in foot in Africa. Or how Islam merchants brought few Atlantean Awakened before in coastal ports. All we go was 'Portugeses follow Atlantis and sometimes local Seprent's Scales themselves also as Mysterium'. Very disappointed here... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-24-2017, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T00:17:41-07:00","id":1067434,"title":"","content":"Mana is a Polynesian concept","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:38:17-07:00","id":1067517,"title":"","content":"Calling mana Vis is such a great callback to the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> I am not sure what to think of the social factions being a localization of the Orders. I'm assuming that it's because of ancient Astral contact with mages from the To The Strongest era forming darshanas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:43:09-07:00","id":1067519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067434#post1067434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana is a Polynesian concept</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to justify it in a setting before Polynesian contact, you could have Mages draw it from the Hebrew (i.e. &quot;Mana from Heaven&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-24-2017, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T05:55:50-07:00","id":1067525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067517#post1067517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure what to think of the social factions being a localization of the Orders. I'm assuming that it's because of ancient Astral contact with mages from the To The Strongest era forming darshanas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>To the Strongest</i> putted Darshanas as one of main Mysteries in the Antiquity<b> MtAw</b> setting. They <i>literally</i> said there whenever are sorceress, they 'instinctual' become Darshanas cults, i.e. more or less based on versions of Diamond Orders. Maybe it's proof for being once upon a time One Atlantis. Or that human societies need 4/5 castes, forever and ever. It's a feature of <b>Awakening</b> 2E setting.<br /> <br /> <b>More concerning to me is lack of text on Portuguese-Mutapa mages contacts.</b> If both groups are 'so similar but different', I would want to read about Tearch Christian missionaries converting natives to Diamond tenets. Or how humble 'soldier' Arrows of Europeans are awestrucked by Sepent's Teeth luxury lives as literal Princes. <i>In other words - for the Era about culture clash, we do <b>not see much of clash of cultures</b></i>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067517#post1067517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling mana Vis is such a great callback to the Order of Hermes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Was it popular in Dark Ages <b>Mage: The Ascension</b>? Like all European Awakened use term <i>Vis</i>?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-24-2017, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:17:42-07:00","id":1067559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067525#post1067525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More concerning to me is lack of text on Portuguese-Mutapa mages contacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be waste of space in a not very long chapter. Also, it pretty explicitly points out the differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:33:05-07:00","id":1067571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067559#post1067559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That'd be waste of space in a not very long chapter. Also, it pretty explicitly points out the differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pointing how Diamond converts native mages - <b>hell no it would be waste. If would direct example as how to run the same events in other Eras. </b>Now it looks like 'Portuguese Awakened come, took some stone statues for Artifacts and left.' And 'Seers are almost nowhere, but they build power structure in poor class'. Nothing about Diamond incorporating other doctrines, nothing about cultural exchange, about Mutapa mage resisting, spread of Atlantean dogma. Nothing. Zero. Zilch. All they point is 'Local Linages use Paths mechanics and Orders are almost the same.' First are almost exactly the same - as they use same mechanics on Arcana - second point how common they are and totally indiffrent.<br /> <br /> Really, from read of <i>Princes of Conquered Lands</i> it would seem that official line on Diamond going to other cultures looks like this: 'Hey, we have awesome Atlantis and your local Orders are totally our own. You just bow to out superior magical theory.'<br /> And natives says: 'Okay' - and in that instance whole country magicians are changed into Diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-24-2017, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:51:37-07:00","id":1067586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067571#post1067571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pointing how Diamond converts native mages - <b>hell no it would be waste. If would direct example as how to run the same events in other Eras. </b>Now it looks like 'Portuguese Awakened come, took some stone statues for Artifacts and left.' And 'Seers are almost nowhere, but they build power structure in poor class'. Nothing about Diamond incorporating other doctrines, nothing about cultural exchange, about Mutapa mage resisting, spread of Atlantean dogma. Nothing. Zero. Zilch. All they point is 'Local Linages use Paths mechanics and Orders are almost the same.' First are almost exactly the same - as they use same mechanics on Arcana - second point how common they are and totally indiffrent.<br /> <br /> Really, from read of <i>Princes of Conquered Lands</i> it would seem that official line on Diamond going to other cultures looks like this: 'Hey, we have awesome Atlantis and your local Orders are totally our own. You just bow to out superior magical theory.'<br /> And natives says: 'Okay' - and in that instance whole country magicians are changed into Diamond. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure where you're reading this. The text states that the Shona beliefs do not die out. They just see less global popularity than the platonic view of magic.<br /> <br /> Also, the more overt clashes are depicted in the Accidental Crusade section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 03-24-2017, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:56:16-07:00","id":1067622,"title":"","content":"I explicitly said...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That'd be waste of space <b>in a not very long chapter.</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And 'Seers are almost nowhere, but they build power structure in poor class'. </div> </div> </div>The lack of Seers is quite odd.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:19:34-07:00","id":1067632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067586#post1067586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure where you're reading this. The text states that the Shona beliefs do not die out. They just see less global popularity than the platonic view of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I really missed this out. Still, I'm more critical in nothing shown as <i>how </i>the Diamond exchange looked like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067586#post1067586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the more overt clashes are depicted in the Accidental Crusade section.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Story Seed about looking couple Diamond and Mutapa mages? It says <b>nothing</b> about how this things would look like. Only 'lock your players and NPCs in one place'. It's based on Sleepers event and only real supernatural thing there is storm.<br /> <br /> As I mentioned before - I'm disappointing not seeing Silver Ladder missionaries convert natives to Diamond, Adamantine Arrows being strucked by local Serpents Teeth takes on fame and poverty, or if Muslim traders where not infiltrated by Diamond and try to make those things earlier. And as posts before - now it looks like 'we meet natives and then we made *poof* Atlantean mages from (most of ) natives'.<br /> <br /> Culture clash consequences are marked in Sleepers section, but they are <i>non-existing</i> in Awakened one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-24-2017, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:30:32-07:00","id":1067645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067632#post1067632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Culture clash consequences are marked in Sleepers section, but they are <i>non-existing</i> in Awakened one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's the point. To The Strongest didn't have the various Great Cults attcking each other either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T09:49:16-07:00","id":1067652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067632#post1067632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I mentioned before - I'm disappointing not seeing Silver Ladder missionaries convert natives to Diamond, Adamantine Arrows being strucked by local Serpents Teeth takes on fame and poverty, or if Muslim traders where not infiltrated by Diamond and try to make those things earlier. And as posts before - now it looks like 'we meet natives and then we made *poof* Atlantean mages from (most of ) natives'.<br /> <br /> Culture clash consequences are marked in Sleepers section, but they are <i>non-existing</i> in Awakened one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tastes are definitely going to vary here. I appreciate that wordcount was spent detailing the Shona beliefs and cultural practices and not on missionaries being grotesque imperialists.<br /> <br /> I do wish we had a little more info on common magical tools for the Shona mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 03-24-2017, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:00:00-07:00","id":1067656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067645#post1067645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's the point. To The Strongest didn't have the various Great Cults attcking each other either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we did not have attacking but highlighted the <i>other</i> interplays of Cults. I really do not need something like 'they kill each other', but more how Diamond made conversions. In <i>To the Strongest</i> it was not said as there were no Diamond then. Here we have unified Orders that goes into new terrain to expand their influances. I really would want to see<i> how </i>Diamond is doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T10:38:10-07:00","id":1067673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067656#post1067656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we did not have attacking but highlighted the <i>other</i> interplays of Cults. I really do not need something like 'they kill each other', but more how Diamond made conversions. In <i>To the Strongest</i> it was not said as there were no Diamond then. Here we have unified Orders that goes into new terrain to expand their influances. I really would want to see<i> how </i>Diamond is doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hang on, why do we know that the Diamond made conversions at all? I don't think this assumption is warranted at all. Here's the section that discusses cross-cultural interactions:<br /> <br /> &quot;Most belong to the Atlantean Diamond, and are educated enough to recognize parallel Orders in the Awakened Mutupos. Sporadic misunderstandings and battles for territory test relations, but Mutapa mages have always paid special attention to the land, and prevent foreigners from seizing magical places.&quot;<br /> <br /> On that same page, it states that the Seer Hegemonic and Paternoster mages are the ones who try to infiltrate under the guise of religious conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T11:41:12-07:00","id":1067712,"title":"","content":"It's a typically... I don't know exactly what it is, but there's a big honking assumption that the &quot;Western&quot; mages conquered other Awakened with blood and attack spells. If India, Arabia, and Northern Africa count as Western in your assumptions, because the native mages of those places were Diamond a couple of centuries earlier than, say, Britain, but that's a digression.<br /> <br /> Is it because of Mage: The Ascension, which linked the movements of its factions to colonialism as a process and tried to link its based-on-90s-club-subcultures factions to &quot;losing sides&quot; in history to give them a sense of background?<br /> <br /> Fuck <i>that</i>. The Awakened are made of sterner stuff. When you habitually deal with things that aren't there but are more True than the common matter around you, and you gained your powers through a brainbending encounter with a Supernal World, another wizard who happens to dress funny is not going to give you pause.<br /> <br /> The Diamond Orders started out when mages of disparate cultures noticed that they had common threads while cooperating to follow their Obsessions. After their formation, another culture having a different-in-some-ways-but-with-common-threads culture is not going to send them into a fit.<br /> <br /> Over time, some Shona mages would join Orders, others would be what later mages would call Nameless. Over more time, the natural processes of &quot;if you're in an Order, you get all this cool stuff&quot; shrank the latter and grew the former. By the modern day, Zimbabwean and Mozambiqan Awakened who try to reconstruct &quot;authentic&quot; Shona magical practices are probably in the Free Council, while the rest are in the Diamond or tiny Nameless Orders. Just like everywhere else.<br /> <br /> No secret wars required.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":28}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T12:07:25-07:00","id":1067724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067712#post1067712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it because of Mage: The Ascension, which linked the movements of its factions to colonialism as a process and tried to link its based-on-90s-club-subcultures factions to &quot;losing sides&quot; in history to give them a sense of background?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is it. In a sense, Ascension (a game about many many things), is at its core a game about cultural survival against the forces of western imperialism.<br /> To support that theme, a lot of the internal conflict in that game is about how the &quot;good guys&quot; of the setting have committed a lot of the same sins as their enemies. For instance, the Order of Hermes disregarded Imperialism in the Middle-East and they rebuffed the Ngoma magi of Northern Africa.<br /> <br /> Awakening is not the same game and has a very different story to tell about cultural exchanges. The Diamond Mages aren't European like the Order of Hermes, and the Awakened Svikiros aren't marginalized sorcerers whose ideas have been erased from a consensual reality.<br /> <br /> It's not that colonialism doesn't exist in Awakening, but it's more of an intentional goal of the Hegemonic ministry, who use it as a magical praxis in order to better serve the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> I really really like both games, and I'm pleased that the writers are distinguishing the settings and themes of each.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":61,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","user":"Octavo","date":". 03-24-2017, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:28:16-07:00","id":1067766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067673#post1067673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hang on, why do we know that the Diamond made conversions at all? I don't think this assumption is warranted at all. Here's the section that discusses cross-cultural interactions:</div> </div> </div> </div>Diamond ( and now Pentacle ) are assume to be global organisations, almost everywhere. Places where Diamond is placed, were logically places where Diamond will be sustained.If we have 100% of native mages 1500s in Mutapa, after years of Diamond contact, at least some XY% will become Diamond. Diamond is based on 'Your own culture is shadow of Atlantis', so logically it would be they would try to convert native mages. And 1E settings - like Boston Unveiled - assumed the same politics of Pentacle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:35:10-07:00","id":1067767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067766#post1067766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diamond ( and now Pentacle ) are assume to be global organisations, almost everywhere. Places where Diamond is placed, were logically places where Diamond will be sustained.If we have 100% of native mages 1500s in Mutapa, after years of Diamond contact, at least some XY% will become Diamond. Diamond is based on 'Your own culture is shadow of Atlantis', so logically it would be they would try to convert native mages. And 1E settings - like Boston Unveiled - assumed the same politics of Pentacle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that ignores what Dave just said, they didn't convert them so much as notice similarities and then ask if they wanted to team up. Native culture would be diluted but not gone via this process. Boston is an exception considering that the arrival of Diamond Mages coincided with the beginning of native genocide by the Sleepers, but it's not the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:40:55-07:00","id":1067768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067712#post1067712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No secret wars required.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said I want to see 'secret wars'. I really get that Diamond done things and expand by diplomacy. I pointed that I wanted to be shown how Diamond would try to convert locals. Will there be Muslims Diamond earlier than Portuguese? How would Arrows react to Serpent's Teethes. Stuff like this. No one said about gunning other side with attack spells - only how Diamond <i>diplomacy </i>works in this cultural exchanges.<br /> <br /> Culture clash does not automatically mean actual fist fighting - only seeing how two cultures will influance each other.<br /> <br /> Seeing it from other perspective - I really would want to play Silver Ladder mage in this kind setting - What would my character do in Mutapa there? Beside 'look for local Mysteries' as it is general answer to <i>any</i> Awakened, not Tearchs only.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-24-2017, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T13:52:10-07:00","id":1067770,"title":"","content":"You could assume that you have a unique chance to see a part of the shattered society you try to reassemble that wasn't discovered by other people like you before, and thus you could show them other things your peers have collected while trying to find their part and learn about it. Cultural exchange, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:09:49-07:00","id":1067778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067770#post1067770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could assume that you have a unique chance to see a part of the shattered society you try to reassemble that wasn't discovered by other people like you before, and thus you could show them other things your peers have collected while trying to find their part and learn about it. Cultural exchange, basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does not sound as 'Star: The Silver Ladder is the Path to Victory'...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:11:25-07:00","id":1067779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067712#post1067712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a typically... I don't know exactly what it is, but there's a big honking assumption that the &quot;Western&quot; mages conquered other Awakened with blood and attack spells. If India, Arabia, and Northern Africa count as Western in your assumptions, because the native mages of those places were Diamond a couple of centuries earlier than, say, Britain, but that's a digression.<br /> <br /> Is it because of Mage: The Ascension, which linked the movements of its factions to colonialism as a process and tried to link its based-on-90s-club-subcultures factions to &quot;losing sides&quot; in history to give them a sense of background?<br /> <br /> Fuck <i>that</i>. The Awakened are made of sterner stuff. When you habitually deal with things that aren't there but are more True than the common matter around you, and you gained your powers through a brainbending encounter with a Supernal World, another wizard who happens to dress funny is not going to give you pause.<br /> <br /> The Diamond Orders started out when mages of disparate cultures noticed that they had common threads while cooperating to follow their Obsessions. After their formation, another culture having a different-in-some-ways-but-with-common-threads culture is not going to send them into a fit.<br /> <br /> Over time, some Shona mages would join Orders, others would be what later mages would call Nameless. Over more time, the natural processes of &quot;if you're in an Order, you get all this cool stuff&quot; shrank the latter and grew the former. By the modern day, Zimbabwean and Mozambiqan Awakened who try to reconstruct &quot;authentic&quot; Shona magical practices are probably in the Free Council, while the rest are in the Diamond or tiny Nameless Orders. Just like everywhere else.<br /> <br /> No secret wars required.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel good that this tracks with my understanding of the setting!<br /> <br /> Bit of a query; I recal from somewhere (not sure where) that Astral travel was always supposed to be a bit of a thing when it came to the spread of the Orders and the connections between Mages around the world, and I always liked the idea too. Mages being naturally inquisitive types, it totally makes sense to me that a Mage in Japan and a Mage in, say, South Africa might meet on an Astral journey, communicate, perhaps share the investigation of a mystery together on the Astral plane, and also share some mystical knowledge that then feeds back and forth. They might even be in there investigating the same mystery feeding into the physical world in their respective locales! This wouldn't happen all the time but it probably would ease the spreading of ideas and concepts through Mage society because, at the end of the day, they all have this ability to explore the Astral and while in there the physical distances between them are irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:13:34-07:00","id":1067780,"title":"","content":"Isn't that percept about social mobility?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:21:39-07:00","id":1067786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067779#post1067779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of a query; I recal from somewhere (not sure where) that Astral travel was always supposed to be a bit of a thing when it came to the spread of the Orders and the connections between Mages around the world, and I always liked the idea too. Mages being naturally inquisitive types, it totally makes sense to me that a Mage in Japan and a Mage in, say, South Africa might meet on an Astral journey, communicate, perhaps share the investigation of a mystery together on the Astral plane, and also share some mystical knowledge that then feeds back and forth. They might even be in there investigating the same mystery feeding into the physical world in their respective locales! This wouldn't happen all the time but it probably would ease the spreading of ideas and concepts through Mage society because, at the end of the day, they all have this ability to explore the Astral and while in there the physical distances between them are irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a common practice in the pre-Sundering era so I imagine it did stick around. The biggest problem is entering a Temenotic realm held by another culture. I imagine, it's not that you can't go there, but that you have to be able to make the right mental associations to pull it off which means you could have a Japanese Mage and a Nordic Mage both visiting the realm of the Sea, and be completely missing each other by accident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T14:30:10-07:00","id":1067791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067778#post1067778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does not sound as 'Star: The Silver Ladder is the Path to Victory'...</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course there is still the Diamond Precept: &quot;The Awakened Are One Nation.&quot; The local, non-Diamond Awakened are not Banishers, nor are they Seers, ergo, they fall under the banner of the glorious Awakened Nation. Even then, Banishers and Seers still have the benefit of protection under the Lex Magica. I don't see the Silver Ladder as the conquering types, especially when it comes to Mages. Their goals are more unification under one banner, are they not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:37:22-07:00","id":1067820,"title":"","content":"The Silver Ladder is not the Path to Victory because they conquer all other Mages, the Silver Ladder is the Path to Victory because they lead other Mages. The real ideal of the Silver Ladder isn't making other Mages serve you through fear (the Lion) or them allowing your weak leadership in lieu of true direction (the Stag) but to display wisdom, knowledge and strength so that others look to you for leadership and guidance (the Sage).<br /> <br /> The common perception amongst many fans about what the Ladder does is kind of misrepresented, I think. They don't rock up to places and say &quot;we're in charge now!&quot; They rock up to places and talk to people, take part in the community, provide systems of law and social understanding, and through actually dedicating themselves to the study of what makes a good leader, they provide leadership and guidance to others. Remember, the Silver Ladder's Atlantean Shadow Name doesn't invoke the Kings and Queens of Atlantis, it invokes the Priests, Judges and Viziers, those honoured for their wisdom, knowledge and just edicts.<br /> <br /> Whether the Silver Ladder has ever actually had an element of monarchism in terms of yearning for the return of the ancient Atlantean Kings and Queens or whatever, I forget. Is that something to do with the Oracles? Regardless, the Ladder is not made up of all conquering imperialist Mages. It's made up of idealists, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:49:59-07:00","id":1067824,"title":"","content":"Silver Ladder and Free Council have a neat dynamic in that both of them will be interested in cultural magic and both might practice or research it, but with very different ideological underpinning. Silver Ladder will look for a reflection of Original Mega Truth hidden inside it, while Free Councilor will insist that &quot;Mega Truth&quot; is a reflection of culture, not the other way around. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:52:31-07:00","id":1067826,"title":"","content":"One thing I've noticed about the Silver Ladder throughout the various books is that they just don't seem to work well if they're played as arrogant schemers who are no better than the Seers. <br /> For me at least, it's easier and more interesting to think of character concepts where they don't suck. At their best they care most about keeping the community of Awakened together than they do about grasping at raw personal power. There's almost something Taoist about the SL when they're doing their sagely thing. They see what has to be done and they do it and then quit when they're done. <br /> <br /> Now I want to play a Silver Ladder based on Eddie Riggs: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vD6dRXIvEU0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vD6dRXIvEU0</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T15:59:30-07:00","id":1067830,"title":"","content":"What I kind of like though is that even though the Ladder sort of see the Free Council as being vaguely parochial and lacking respect, and the Council see the Ladder as being vaguely stuffy and arrogant, the Pentacle definitely isn't an alliance of convenience these days and they do actually share a lot of viewpoints that could practically translate into working together.<br /> <br /> The cultural magic they are interested in they come at from different angles, but at the end of the day, they're both looking for pretty much the same ideal; that magic to be freed from the Lie. Of all the Orders/Sects, they are the two most opposed to the Seers who are the enforcers of the Lie, of all the Orders/Sects, they are the most interested in actually improving the lot of Sleepers (because both of them believe, in general, that the freer mortals are from the most brutal and crushing aspects of the Lie, the more likely they are to seek the Truth), of all the Orders/Sects, they are the ones most interested in actually giving Mages a voice and a way of resolving issues in society. They disagree on how to do that but they both agree, more than the others, that such a system should definitely be there.<br /> <br /> The core ideals of the Silver Ladder and the Free Council differ in rhetoric substantially, and they ostensibly differ quite a bit in reality too, but in reality, I found that in our games, Free Council Mages and Silver Ladder Mages often found their viewpoint on any particular subject aligning, especially when it came to matters of how Mages should act towards Sleepers etc. That was quite cool, and I dunno if it's intentional or if I'm just reading into it too much, but I do like that what are on the surface the two most opposed elements of the Pentacle actually might find themselves agreeing in practise on a lot of policy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:34:34-07:00","id":1067838,"title":"","content":"They were the closest allies among any Pentacle Orders. At least until the Free Council fucked it up. And that only happened in America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:39:33-07:00","id":1067840,"title":"","content":"&quot;Silver Ladder x Free Council&quot; is one of most natural and easiest to write crossovers in the Pentacle. It's really easy to write a Ladder NPC that will find themselves at home no matter if we are talking about Consilium or Assembly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T16:53:52-07:00","id":1067842,"title":"","content":"I've always compared The Silver Ladder to Hufflepuff House. They are by far the most loyal of the Orders, and the most optimistic. They believe in Awakening for <i>everyone</i>, and work to bring the Awakened together as One Nation Under The Supernal. They believe in the Diamond (and the Pentacle) the most, and in humanity's inherent potential to ascend. The only reason you might view them as stuffy or arrogant is if you don't agree with them in their beliefs, in which case they might come across as dogmatic and pushy or patronizing. But given that I 100% agree with The Silver Ladder, I've always seen them as sort of like Mahayana Buddhists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T17:34:50-07:00","id":1067855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067842#post1067842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always compared The Silver Ladder to Hufflepuff House. They are by far the most loyal of the Orders, and the most optimistic. They believe in Awakening for <i>everyone</i>, and work to bring the Awakened together as One Nation Under The Supernal. They believe in the Diamond (and the Pentacle) the most, and in humanity's inherent potential to ascend. The only reason you might view them as stuffy or arrogant is if you don't agree with them in their beliefs, in which case they might come across as dogmatic and pushy or patronizing. But given that I 100% agree with The Silver Ladder, I've always seen them as sort of like Mahayana Buddhists.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, it was always Ladder=Slytherin, Mysterium=Ravenclaw, Arrows=Gryffindor, Council=Hufflepuff and I dunno, I guess Guardians are the outsiders, maybe the Aurors (and in an ideal Awakened society they don't have a place at all, thanks to the Abyss not existing anymore). I mean, the Hufflepuff literally take in &quot;the rest&quot;, those not fitting into any other House, just like what often happens when new mages are recruited into the Council . The difference from Potterverse is that Slytherins strive to be the paragons of leadership and want to protect the Muggles and somehow remake them into mages and the Death Eaters are a terrorist faction inside Ravenclaw (*cough* Daksha and Jnanamukti *cough*).<br /> <br /> Besides, [proud Thearch exclamation] <b>Merlin was a Thearch.</b> [/proud Thearch exclamation]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","user":"Prometheus","date":". 03-24-2017, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T18:09:27-07:00","id":1067874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067855#post1067855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, it was always Ladder=Slytherin, Mysterium=Ravenclaw, Arrows=Gryffindor, Council=Hufflepuff and I dunno, I guess Guardians are the outsiders, maybe the Aurors (and in an ideal Awakened society they don't have a place at all, thanks to the Abyss not existing anymore). I mean, the Hufflepuff literally take in &amp;quot;the rest&amp;quot;, those not fitting into any other House, just like what often happens when new mages are recruited into the Council . The difference from Potterverse is that Slytherins strive to be the paragons of leadership and want to protect the Muggles and somehow remake them into mages and the Death Eaters are a terrorist faction inside Ravenclaw (*cough* Daksha and Jnanamukti *cough*).<br /> <br /> Besides, [proud Thearch exclamation] <b>Merlin was a Thearch.</b> [/proud Thearch exclamation]</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmm, that's the Hogwarts house/Pentacle pairing I went with in my Potterverse game. I finessed the houses a bit so the Slytherins had less of a monopoly on moral failings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T18:27:55-07:00","id":1067879,"title":"","content":"Mine was always<br /> <br /> Arrow - Gryffindor<br /> Mysterium - Ravenclaw<br /> Ladder - Hufflepuff<br /> Guardians - Slytherin<br /> <br /> and the Free Council says 'fuck your Harry Potter bullshit.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T23:00:06-07:00","id":1067927,"title":"","content":"Returning to topic - I feel lack of pointing things like that in Mutapa Era text. From read of corebooks and some <b>Silver Ladder</b> Order book - <b>ESPECIALLY their love for British Empire</b> - I'm confused over the means they employ in to 'talking over' native mages. More - <b>How the rest of Diamond will treat natives?</b> Silver Ladder maybe all about 'we should be Sage', but we still have Adamantine Arrows, Misterium and Guardians doing SOMETHING in new ( to Europeans ) land. Will they steal local Artifacts and say 'their mine, I found it'? Will they show 'You need Lex Magica as we operate under it and it only will ends raids of our Diamond brothers'? Excuse me, but I'm not optimistic at meeting two civilizations of sorcerers that will all go nice, fluffy and wonderful. They may not go over knives, but Europeans are there not to sea-sighting ( they have Sapce for that ), but to do some goals there - most of them would be 'To get their nice and juicy Mysteries'.<br /> <br /> Also, should not some Diamond native mages already greet European mages, as Muslims made some converts from <i>centuries</i> of trade exchange with Shona?<br /> <br /> I did not found any of things in Era text ( or even contrary assumptions on those matters, as those would be answers too ), only 'Seers are in secret, building their power base', so I feel it's missed opportunity in all Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T23:55:09-07:00","id":1067936,"title":"","content":"Awesome era! I really appreciate time time taken to flesh out the various types of spirits and Svikiro in Mutapa. Super glad you dedicated so much time to them, it certainly feels like I learned something that was authentic about a culture of which I previously knew next to nothing. Definitely the highlight of the Era. Much like Sundered World, there is enough general information here that I would feel comfortable running most gamelines in this era. Crossover mechanics were really interesting. Not surprised that most of your sources had to be academic journals, there are precious few popular books about the Empire. Good news is that there seem to be a descent number of sources on JSTOR, which you can get limited free access to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T01:35:12-07:00","id":1067946,"title":"","content":"One of Malcolm's friends happens to have her doctorate in African history - she helped us a bit with To The Strongest, and a <i>lot</i> with Princes of the Conquered Land. Like calling the people of the time &quot;Shona&quot; despite them not, technically, being Shona as the modern world knows them. Eric, Malcolm, and I are really indebted to her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T03:05:35-07:00","id":1067953,"title":"","content":"Returning to my problems with his Era - I was <i>really </i>looking for even sidebar that would point what European mages would do in there, split by Diamond Orders. Something like this:<ul><li><b>Adamantine Arrow</b> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conquistador\" target=\"_blank\">Conqistadors </a>- soldiers and explorers - trying to get new land for Portugal. Later, becoming Arrows become archeomancers and guardians of zimbabwe ruins.</li> <li><b>Guardians of Veil </b>\u2013 Nothing comes to me here beside \u2018Portuguese spies\u2019 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></li> <li><b>Mysterium </b>\u2013 Explorers and reserchers, looking for Atlantean traces.</li> <li><b>Silver Ladder</b> - Misionaries and priests of Church, converting Shona and showing them principles of Atlantis. Traders making contracts and secret Cryptopolies in new land.</li> </ul>Not to mention lack of Muslim Diamond in text at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Era is written like only Shona Awakened took part in this events. We do not see any Diamond side on matter. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-25-2017, 07:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T04:16:43-07:00","id":1067960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067953#post1067953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]<b>Guardians of Veil </b>\u2013 Nothing comes to me her beside \u2018Spanish spies\u2019 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't you mean Portuguese?<br /> <br /> Presumably the Guardians follow the other Orders, that's part of their mission to watch the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T04:43:34-07:00","id":1067963,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I fixed. Idea of sidebar was to give basic European characters concepts from Orders. So 'Guardians are watching' is not helpfull as it's not character concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:18:08-07:00","id":1067969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067963#post1067963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idea of sidebar was to give basic European characters concepts from Orders. So 'Guardians are watching' is not helpfull as it's not character concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither are the things you wrote.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:20:09-07:00","id":1067971,"title":"","content":"And killing off the Left-Handed, and performing all their other functions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:39:03-07:00","id":1067975,"title":"","content":"Also, there's the quasi-theology of the Guardians that seems to be absent from the Serpent's Eyes. The Silver Ladder aren't the only people out to convert people.<br /> <br /> Actually, it's not all that clear to me whether the underlying philosophy of the Orders is meant to be similiar but unstated, or it's meant to be absent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T16:07:19-07:00","id":1068116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067838#post1067838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were the closest allies among any Pentacle Orders. At least until the Free Council fucked it up. And that only happened in America.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall what happened there to be honest. Is it in an order book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T16:36:36-07:00","id":1068120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1068116#post1068116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall what happened there to be honest. Is it in an order book?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in Mage Noir. The SL and FC cooperated after WW2 to get members of the Orders out of the remains of the German Empire.<br /> <br /> However, members of the FC used it as cover to reintegrate members of Pantechnicon. (Which the SL probably should have seen coming, but whatever)<br /> <br /> It ends badly when the Guardians reveal it. The two orders fall out very badly, though who exactly is worse depends on whether you think Nazi Thearchs or Seers are worse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T17:07:57-07:00","id":1068124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1068120#post1068120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in Mage Noir. The SL and FC cooperated after WW2 to get members of the Orders out of the remains of the German Empire.<br /> <br /> However, members of the FC used it as cover to reintegrate members of Pantechnicon. (Which the SL probably should have seen coming, but whatever)<br /> <br /> It ends badly when the Guardians reveal it. The two orders fall out very badly, though who exactly is worse depends on whether you think Nazi Thearchs or Seers are worse.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Silver Ladder didn't exactly endear themselves too anyone secretly saving Nazi mages.<br /> <br /> The Guardians surprisingly screwed-up the least during WWII.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T21:26:07-07:00","id":1068541,"title":"","content":"It occurs to me that a possible interpretation of how the Shona mages are guided by Mhondoros from each path is that those Supernal Entities are in fact ascended beings or possibly even Oracles. For instance, Dzivaguru is said to appear in any gender (much like an Exarch whose identity has been worn away by the Supernal). &quot;The other Mhondoro rose from history that became myth, but Dzivaguru\u2019s legend comes from before all history.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T01:41:44-07:00","id":1068582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1068120#post1068120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in Mage Noir. The SL and FC cooperated after WW2 to get members of the Orders out of the remains of the German Empire.<br /> <br /> However, members of the FC used it as cover to reintegrate members of Pantechnicon. (Which the SL probably should have seen coming, but whatever)<br /> <br /> It ends badly when the Guardians reveal it. The two orders fall out very badly, though who exactly is worse depends on whether you think Nazi Thearchs or Seers are worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm so the Free Council were integrating Seers? That seems like it would definitely cause a rift with most Ladders! Interesting little fact there. Though my CofD games are usually set outside the US these days, so I imagine the FC and SL get on well in other places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T04:32:44-07:00","id":1068608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1068582#post1068582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though my CofD games are usually set outside the US these days, so I imagine the FC and SL get on well in other places.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno about Dave's official version, but I don't really see it. I mean, unlike the Diamond Orders, the FC has genuine ambitions to replace the consilia system. That directly flys in the face of the SL who effectively run that system.<br /> <br /> Personally, the SL inviting the FC to join the Pentacle looks a lot less like an idealistic move, and more like a clever co-option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:20:55-07:00","id":1068827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1067712#post1067712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a typically... I don't know exactly what it is, but there's a big honking assumption that the &quot;Western&quot; mages conquered other Awakened with blood and attack spells. If India, Arabia, and Northern Africa count as Western in your assumptions, because the native mages of those places were Diamond a couple of centuries earlier than, say, Britain, but that's a digression.<br /> <br /> Is it because of Mage: The Ascension, which linked the movements of its factions to colonialism as a process and tried to link its based-on-90s-club-subcultures factions to &quot;losing sides&quot; in history to give them a sense of background?</div> </div> </div> </div>Realtalk, I've never read Ascension and only read Awakening 2e for the first time like a month and a half ago but I was definitely on this mental train because to me Mages may have their secret society but are still humans and live lives embedded in society which has its own ups and downs and twists. I'd always figured there'd be a fair amount of mages in any given nation who go along with a war or something because that's where they live and they're still people who were raised in Portugal or the British Empire or whatever.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the Diamond comes from places aside from traditional western powers but then it was European colonialism that spread Europeans and their militaries the world over. It kind of seemed natural that mages from those nations would follow along, not unlike how vampires did as parasites riding ahead and in the wake and often times run into local vampires. But you know, without the parasite or predator imagery.<br /> <br /> Obviously that's not what you are thinking so I was wrong, but I don't think it is entirely unreasonable a view to have had without having to pin it on old familiarity with Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T15:33:14-07:00","id":1068904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1068608#post1068608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno about Dave's official version, but I don't really see it. I mean, unlike the Diamond Orders, the FC has genuine ambitions to replace the consilia system. That directly flys in the face of the SL who effectively run that system.<br /> <br /> Personally, the SL inviting the FC to join the Pentacle looks a lot less like an idealistic move, and more like a clever co-option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but hey, at least they care. Like, it's a common fallacy in political science conversations that everyone falls on the political spectrum; some people literally don't give a shit. The Silver Ladder (as a generalised organisational view) spends all it's time saying &quot;fight the Lie! The Lie is shit and the Seers are total bastards! Achieve enlightenment! Grasp ascension! Let us unify and be free!&quot; and the Mysterium, Guardians and Arrow are all varying degrees of &quot;that's not really our core philosophy but sure yeah I guess, if I'm free.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Free Council enthusiastically say the same thing. They disagree how to do it, they disagree on how to organise Mage society and how to inspire Sleepers etc, but their core ideas are all about fighting the Lie, freeing Sleepers from Quiescience, overcoming the Seers and their Exarch masters, giving Mages a voice and a chance to fulfill their potential etc. That's the whole deal with the Great Refusal.<br /> <br /> So while the Free Council and the Silver Ladder might have a number of ostensible idealogical differences, and a number of ostensible practical ones too, in reality for a lot of Silver Ladder and Free Council Mages they find themselves caring about the same things. And while the Ladder says &quot;look at this cultural Magic, isn't it cool how they managed to capture a fragment of the Supernal Truth!&quot; and the Council says &quot;no, the Supernal Truth is created by Cultural Magic!&quot; in reality they're both kind of right, and both are actually interested in trying to help Sleepers reach the Supernal, just via different structural systems.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Assembly is posited as an alternative is something that threatens the Ladder's position as the Order with the most political sway, but at the same time, the Concilium system works in ways the Assembly system doesn't, and it's more likely that they'll find a degree of balance based on the location rather than anything else. Remember, the strength of the Consilium is that it accepts that Mages are not all equal and powerful Mages at the top ensure a society which is ordered enough for people to live in, and even the Free Council sometimes have to accept that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T16:20:04-07:00","id":1068927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah but hey, at least they care. </div> </div> </div>Let me rephrase a little. It's certainly possible that the SL and FC could come to be very close due to certain similarities, however I think it ultimately requires one side to seriously compromise itself, and it generally looks like the FC are the ones doing that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while the Ladder says &quot;look at this cultural Magic, isn't it cool how they managed to capture a fragment of the Supernal Truth!&quot; and the Council says &quot;no, the Supernal Truth is created by Cultural Magic!&quot; in reality they're both kind of right, and both are actually interested in trying to help Sleepers reach the Supernal, just via different structural systems. </div> </div> </div>I agree it kinda looks that way from the readers perspective (writing made-up ideologies is hard), but if it were that simple then the characters in the setting would be morons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1068904#post1068904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, the strength of the Consilium is that it accepts that Mages are not all equal and powerful Mages at the top ensure a society which is ordered enough for people to live in, and even the Free Council sometimes have to accept that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a Hierarchy. I'm not disagreeing that they accept it, they clearly do, but that's still a very deep compromise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T16:35:15-07:00","id":1068931,"title":"","content":"I don't think the characters in the setting are morons, which is why by and large I tend to find the FC and SL get on well, sharing a desire to promote and invest in Sleeper towards the kind of situation where they are more likely to Awaken, away from the Lie. That's very much something they'd agree on, and a big part of each order's philosophy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T16:55:29-07:00","id":1068937,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar117_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"117\" data-vbnamecard=\"117\">Solar</a>. Just because the Assembly system creates a democratic system of government as opposed to the &quot;meritocratic&quot; consilium system doesn't mean that the Free Council is going to throw the baby out with the bathwater. They may still incorporate many aspects of the Lex Magica, and the Silver Ladder's main calling is making sure that the Awakened are united and cooperating, not 'ruling' them. (That seems far more like the Seers.) So there may still be plenty of Silver Ladder in an Assembly-run city who serve as representation in Assembly for those who feel overwhelmed or anxious, or simply being mediators between Cabals.<br /> <br /> There's this idea in Mage, which I think was more justified in 1e, that the Silver Ladder are the &quot;wizard Ventrue&quot; or the &quot;wizard Invictus&quot; and I'm not really sure I see it, especially not in 2e. In 2e, they are more idealists than overlords.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that the Diamond would not have joined with the Free Council and formed the Pentacle if they hadn't felt that there would be something to gain from the union, and vice versa. It's not just their mutual hatred of the Seers that keeps them together. Both see their cooperation as being for the benefit of Awakened society as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T18:17:06-07:00","id":1068961,"title":"","content":"... and Libertines are cultural mages that want to recreate 'original' native spellcasting practices that Silver Ladder made with 'Atlantis this, Atlantis that, you are only shadows of our great magical heritage' nearly extinct. However Tearchs want's their's on top, in the end they try to unified everything <i>too much</i>, going over to clash with Free Council on most base matters.<br /> <br /> So Silver Ladder, on the side, ARE 'wizards Ventrue' - they want to run a show and make a system that will promote their own ideas. It's much more less than Requiem Ventrues, but it's there.<br /> <br /> And I really miss this Era text do not discuss this subject in any way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-27-2017, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:24:33-07:00","id":1068984,"title":"","content":"They are nothing as the Ventrue. They're the opposite. Thearchs are humanists, they are the champions of humankind. In their words, each Sleeper suffering is a sign the thearchs has still not succeed in their goal. And their goal is the humanity.<br /> <br /> There are thearchs that ressemble Ventrue. Absolutelly. But those are lions thearchs, but the role of the thearch is not that. Theymust be the sages, who guide and lead the human race to divinity.<br /> <br /> I loved SL orderbook. It changed my perception of SL from wizard-Ventrue to idealist champions of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 03-28-2017, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T19:28:33-07:00","id":1068985,"title":"","content":"SL: We will lead humanity to enlightenment<br /> <br /> FC: Humanity will lead us to enlightenment","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T20:16:28-07:00","id":1069004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1068961#post1068961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... and Libertines are cultural mages that want to recreate 'original' native spellcasting practices that Silver Ladder made with 'Atlantis this, Atlantis that, you are only shadows of our great magical heritage' nearly extinct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, you're describing a cultural genocide which has never actually been an institutional thing that exists. The Atlantean contextual framework that the Silver Ladder has been assembling and refining for centuries as part of the ongoing project that is the Precept of Diamond says that there is a timeless underpinning of reality that Important Things tap into as an emergent phenomenon, whereas the Council of Free Assemblies contends that Important Things have a connection to the symbolic core of common reality because it is in the nature of human activity and experience to make Important Things.<br /> <br /> The extent of elitism present in this dichotomy is that the Diamond places less importance on a unified cultural style compared to the more universal/individualistic model they've been piecing together since Alexander, because the rest is ultimately no more a bunch of optional dress-up than anything else a mage does to draw upon celestial might and reshape the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T23:42:35-07:00","id":1069155,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> , literally cannot understand what you writing here. I suspect that something to 'Tearchs make less unified culture than was presented in 1E because they understand that each culture have a shared of Truth in it' - on to what I would answer - they still push 'Atlantean' culture where they are. At least from what I understand changes in 2E corebook of Orders, Silver Ladders are <i>evangelists</i> of Atlantis in Pentacle. They seek Atlantean lore to point 'See? There WAS some common Atlantis, we have right'.<br /> <br /> Which <b>is</b>, in long play, cultural colonialism. Like Christianity said they were always right about spiritual matters and local native faiths are lie. Or how we all speak English just because in XVIII and XIX century British Empire spanning half of world. If your own culture - in this example 'Atlantean' one - expels one of local people - it is <i>still</i> colonialism. With less bullets and spells, but non the less they are taking believes of foreign cultures over theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-28-2017, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T00:19:00-07:00","id":1069175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069155#post1069155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that something to 'Tearchs make less unified culture than was presented in 1E because they understand that each culture have a shared of Truth in it' - on to what I would answer - they still push 'Atlantean' culture where they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <i>is </i>no &quot;Atlantean culture.&quot; &quot;Atlantean culture&quot; is the common ground the Diamond has been finding and building on since its formation along with whatever significant finds they can get out of the ruins, aside from the Ladder's focus on Unifying Magical Civilization the worldview is largely content to exist on its own \u2014 mages have ways of letting information stick around that doesn't require complete regional saturation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least from what I understand changes in 2E corebook of Orders, Silver Ladders are <i>evangelists</i> of Atlantis in Pentacle. They seek Atlantean lore to point 'See? There WAS some common Atlantis, we have right'. </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, it's just possible that the main goal of the folks who're building an enlightened nation out of shared cultural foundations and magical archaeology are after Atlantean lore first and foremost to better put together what Atlantean lore can help them build an enlightened nation before any &quot;See, see!&quot; posturing about justifying the existence of Convocations and the Consilium \u2014 the th\u00e9archs being pegged as the Political Order in fandom thought doesn't negate the fact that they're a bunch of mages with an area of inquiry and a shared long-term project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which <b>is</b>, in long play, cultural colonialism. </div> </div> </div>That would be cultural genocide you're talking about. The Ladder existing and promoting a view of the Tellurian that's stuck around for a while does not inherently constitute an attempt to quash competing cultures; you may notice that attempts to subvert smaller Nameless Orders and similar behaviors aren't presented as common tactics by any party apart from technically the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T02:35:59-07:00","id":1069211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1068931#post1068931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the characters in the setting are morons,</div> </div> </div> </div>But you do think they can't see that their philosophies are essentially the same. Or perhaps you think they do think they're just the same, which I don't really see any evidence of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's this idea in Mage, which I think was more justified in 1e, that the Silver Ladder are the &quot;wizard Ventrue&quot; or the &quot;wizard Invictus&quot; and I'm not really sure I see it, especially not in 2e. In 2e, they are more idealists than overlords. </div> </div> </div>I've never understood why they had to be either. They're authoritarian legalists, that's what they are. It's even outright stated that when they're working democratically, they still pretend that they're an autocracy where the deacon calls the shots. But that doesn't make them not idealists, well intentioned or maybe even right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So there may still be plenty of Silver Ladder in an Assembly-run city who serve as representation in Assembly for those who feel overwhelmed or anxious, or simply being mediators between Cabals. </div> </div> </div>That may well be true, but it's again, a massive compromise of their beliefs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, remember that the Diamond would not have joined with the Free Council and formed the Pentacle if they hadn't felt that there would be something to gain from the union, and vice versa. It's not just their mutual hatred of the Seers that keeps them together. Both see their cooperation as being for the benefit of Awakened society as a whole. </div> </div> </div>They do. They end the Nameless War. My point is that the SL decision doesn't have to be seen as by any means idealistic. It makes sense, if you have a massive group who will not integrate themselves into an order, to give them their own order if it means they'll generally submit to the consilia system. I mean, it's a pretty classic way to fight revolutionaries, give them a party and co-opt them.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not saying that that's bad, merely that it's a compromise between two groups who ultimately have quite different objectives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T03:05:54-07:00","id":1069221,"title":"","content":"Consilium isn't government. It's a Legal System for deciding arguments between mages, that often serves as government-substitute. A Heirarch is not a Prince.<br /> <br /> What do Ladder do when they've signed up and believe in an Assembly? They get stuck into making &quot;we take democratic vites on everything!&quot; work, including a legal system more nuanced that mob justice, advocacy for loners, and throw themselves into the &quot;make Sleepers lives better&quot; part of their beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T03:21:50-07:00","id":1069225,"title":"","content":"The Silver Ladder invokes the concepts of Atlantean Judges, Viziers, Lawyers, Advisors, Priests and Civil Servants. A Democracy can, in fact needs, all those things. The idea behind the Consilium is to make Mage society livable in and give Mages legal protection and a voice, not to dominate all Mages.<br /> <br /> An Assembly doesn't really do that, in fact, and honestly the end point of the Assembly/Consilium situation probably looks like a democratic Assembly of Mages fulfilling the substitute government role at times, and the Consilium fulfilling the legal system role when needed. It's hardly like the idea of separating your government and legal system is a novel one.<br /> <br /> The Pentacle is an impressive and ultimately unified force for more than just reasons of &quot;need to band against the Seers.&quot; They also share ideals and goals. The Free Council and Silver Ladder are ostensibly very different, as I've repeatedly said, but in practicality they have a lot to be getting on with together and not grudgingly so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T04:53:13-07:00","id":1069250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069225#post1069225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Ladder invokes the concepts of Atlantean Judges, Viziers, Lawyers, Advisors, Priests and Civil Servants. A Democracy can, in fact needs, all those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who says? I mean, you're lumping in a large number of varied roles there. The FC is a direct democracy of a tiny number of people; it's not obvious it does need lawyers, judges or civil servants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea behind the Consilium is to make Mage society livable in and give Mages legal protection and a voice, not to dominate all Mages. </div> </div> </div>I feel that misses how politics works. Whatever the idealistic intentions, the reality is that it still forms an unelected oligarchy of more powerful Awakened who are then called to settle disputes over which they have a vested interest. Sure, that's certainly workable and the SL do a good job making the thing work, but that doesn't change the fact that the underlying structure flies in the face of the FCs beliefs and is very open to corruption.<br /> <br /> Plus, in many cases it doesn't work. There's clearly plenty of corruption. I mean, the SL have an entire section of their ideology devoted to their members going off the rails. That would seem to indicate that it's a live issue for them that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's hardly like the idea of separating your government and legal system is a novel one. </div> </div> </div>It's possible, it's just that there's clearly a preference against it. The Assembly is generally just the FC and a few associates. If the SL thought they were a good idea, then they'd join them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Pentacle is an impressive and ultimately unified force for more than just reasons of &quot;need to band against the Seers.&quot; They also share ideals and goals. The Free Council and Silver Ladder are ostensibly very different, as I've repeatedly said, but in practicality they have a lot to be getting on with together and not grudgingly so. </div> </div> </div>I think there's a difference between the individual Thearchs and the Orders as a whole. Individually I think you're right, as Orders I think they're pretty irrevocably against each other on a number of fairly fundamental issues. Further, those kinds of tensions are what drives stories, where you can't just claim that everyone is on the same side and end it there.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean they need to knife each other in the back, but neither should their differences be played down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T07:16:14-07:00","id":1069322,"title":"","content":"After all this discussion about the Silver Ladder and the Free Council, I really am becoming curious about whether the Nameless War will get a full treatment in either Tome of the Pentacle or the unannounced book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:01:16-07:00","id":1069356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069322#post1069322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all this discussion about the Silver Ladder and the Free Council, I really am becoming curious about whether the Nameless War will get a full treatment in either Tome of the Pentacle or the unannounced book.</div> </div> </div> </div>For such a monumental event, it's been given a surprising lack of space. I mean, the causes are vague and to an extent implied, which I suspect is where this back and forth on the SL-FC relations is coming from. It'd be really good to see a clear picture of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:06:30-07:00","id":1069360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069356#post1069356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For such a monumental event, it's been given a surprising lack of space. I mean, the causes are vague and to an extent implied, which I suspect is where this back and forth on the SL-FC relations is coming from. It'd be really good to see a clear picture of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was at first very excited to see that the Reconstruction Dark Era referred to the Nameless War, but it kinda forgot to say who the local Nameless were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:15:40-07:00","id":1069364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069250#post1069250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that misses how politics works. Whatever the idealistic intentions, the reality is that it still forms an unelected oligarchy of more powerful Awakened who are then called to settle disputes over which they have a vested interest. Sure, that's certainly workable and the SL do a good job making the thing work, but that doesn't change the fact that the underlying structure flies in the face of the FCs beliefs and is very open to corruption.<br /> <br /> Plus, in many cases it doesn't work. There's clearly plenty of corruption. I mean, the SL have an entire section of their ideology devoted to their members going off the rails. That would seem to indicate that it's a live issue for them that</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAssemblies are not free from exactly the same sorts of issues; direct democracy is just as prone to corruption, power brokering, and additionally adds issues of majority oppression of minority groups without restraint. Vote buying and favor trading is a huge issue in small direct democracies. Silver Ladder opposition is largely rooted in these issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there's a difference between the individual Thearchs and the Orders as a whole. Individually I think you're right, as Orders I think they're pretty irrevocably against each other on a number of fairly fundamental issues. Further, those kinds of tensions are what drives stories, where you can't just claim that everyone is on the same side and end it there.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean they need to knife each other in the back, but neither should their differences be played down. </div> </div> </div>I think the differences are far less fundamental than that. The Orders have much more in common with each other than they do anyone else. They're both trying to build a better Awakened society, they're both concerned with the treatment of Sleepers, they both want to spread access and awareness of magic and the Supernal in a way that make the other Orders nervous, they both strongly oppose the Seers. They differ on tactics and philosophy for achieving the same ends, but their practical objectives are generally aligned. When push comes to shove they're much more likely to support each other than not, especially in moments of actual crisis. And then go back to bitterly arguing philosophy over which approach is actually better once the moment has passed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T08:53:11-07:00","id":1069389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069364#post1069364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAssemblies are not free from exactly the same sorts of issues; direct democracy is just as prone to corruption, power brokering, and additionally adds issues of majority oppression of minority groups without restraint. Vote buying and favor trading is a huge issue in small direct democracies. Silver Ladder opposition is largely rooted in these issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a question of whether the Assembly is actually better or not, it's a matter of what the FC think. The fact is, they clearly do have massive issues with the consilium structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T10:05:43-07:00","id":1069428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069389#post1069389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a question of whether the Assembly is actually better or not, it's a matter of what the FC think. The fact is, they clearly do have massive issues with the consilium structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have an issue with the consilium structure in principle though, they have issues with individual consilia in implementation. There are consilia that are structured as representative democracies, and the FC are explicitly called out as being able to function in them just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T10:11:36-07:00","id":1069436,"title":"","content":"There are also indirect democracy Assemblies where voters acknowledge they don't have know-how to make smart decisions, so they directly empower people they believe to be skilled and wise so they make these decisions for them.<br /> Important part is that these representatives and rulers need to be backed by the voters, obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T12:04:15-07:00","id":1069522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069221#post1069221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consilium isn't government. It's a Legal System for deciding arguments between mages, that often serves as government-substitute. A Heirarch is not a Prince.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference?<br /> <br /> I ask that seriously. If the role of the Hierarch and Council is to make, maintain, and mediate laws, what differentiates them from a government? They might not resemble a modern government but they fit the bill at least as well as any medieval state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069221#post1069221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do Ladder do when they've signed up and believe in an Assembly? They get stuck into making &amp;quot;we take democratic vites on everything!&amp;quot; work, including a legal system more nuanced that mob justice, advocacy for loners, and throw themselves into the &amp;quot;make Sleepers lives better&amp;quot; part of their beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is, I think, the first time you've framed Mages in a positive light.<br /> <br /> It feels... Weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T12:14:41-07:00","id":1069530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is, I think, the first time you've framed Mages in a positive light.<br /> <br /> It feels... Weird.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, he's also talked about how the SL takes direct aim at the things that hinder upward social mobility and attempts to blow them out of the water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T12:27:12-07:00","id":1069539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069522#post1069522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's the difference?<br /> <br /> I ask that seriously. If the role of the Hierarch and Council is to make, maintain, and mediate laws, what differentiates them from a government? They might not resemble a modern government but they fit the bill at least as well as any medieval state.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that in 2E, consilium is more of an ad hoc thing. They don't enforce laws so much as they mediate disputes based on precedence. Mages don't have to have permits for their wands as in Fantastic Beasts, but if someone's trying to horn in on that Mystery you're diligently investigating, you can appeal to the consilium before anyone ends up dead. <br /> <br /> If a Vampire court is Versailles in the era of Louis the XVI, then the Consilium is Night Court with duels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T13:03:58-07:00","id":1069560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069539#post1069539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that in 2E, consilium is more of an ad hoc thing. They don't enforce laws so much as they mediate disputes based on precedence. Mages don't have to have permits for their wands as in Fantastic Beasts, but if someone's trying to horn in on that Mystery you're diligently investigating, you can appeal to the consilium before anyone ends up dead.<br /> <br /> If a Vampire court is Versailles in the era of Louis the XVI, then the Consilium is Night Court with duels.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are Sentinels for if not enforcing laws? What use is the Consilium if they don't enforce their edicts and mandates? If you petition the Consilium about that annoying Acanthus aggressively asserting authority over an abstruse artifact in your aegis, what does it matter if they don't actually <i>do</i> anything when they rule in your favour? Their words would have all the weight of the UN Maritime Court has at the moment in the South China Sea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T13:17:03-07:00","id":1069574,"title":"","content":"If you decide to stop paying taxes, your government will put you into jail, and you may not decide to stop being a citizen and still live there. <br /> Consilium will tax you and expect you to obey it's law...but it's up to you if you want to subscribe. You join wanting benefits, and in exchange you are expected to follow Consiliums guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:06:49-07:00","id":1069610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069560#post1069560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are Sentinels for if not enforcing laws? What use is the Consilium if they don't enforce their edicts and mandates? If you petition the Consilium about that annoying Acanthus aggressively asserting authority over an abstruse artifact in your aegis, what does it matter if they don't actually <i>do</i> anything when they rule in your favour? Their words would have all the weight of the UN Maritime Court has at the moment in the South China Sea.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make some good points. A Consilium has laws and it sometimes makes laws, although I suspect it's more like an accumulation of case law than it is a formal legislative process (that probably happens at Convocations). It also sends out Sentinels who are half detective, half bailiff and usually wield the Lex Magica merit in order to enforce rulings. I think what makes a consilium different than sleeper municipal governments is that they're volunteers who only really gather together when they need to. There probably aren't regular Royal Courts with intrigues and gossip. They're also not parliaments or cabinets that frequently meet to make policy. There aren't tax collectors or audits or permits. I suspect they're more modeled after academic boards than municipal councils.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:21:57-07:00","id":1069618,"title":"","content":"Yeah, imagine you are in a conflict with another Mage. If that Mage is a member of Consilium, Consilium will try to mediate the conflict, and if it doesn't work, it might ask either of you to act in certain way or accept a certain ruling; you either do that, or you exclude yourself from the benefits that being a member of community provides. <br /> <br /> If that Mage isn't a member of Consilium, then Consilium might still go and mediate for you...but it also might just punch the Mage in the face and take his stuff to give it to you, because it has no obligations towards that wizard. By refusing to congregate, they aren't one of &quot;ours&quot;, so no protection for them. <br /> A big difference between Free Council and Silver Ladder might be that Silver Ladder says that all Mages should have rights and privelieges in the Consilium, kinda like we agree that there are certain human rights that cannot be revoked or abandoned, even willingly. Free Council at it's worst might embrace &quot;US&quot; and &quot;NOT US&quot; philosophy to the brutal extreme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T14:48:08-07:00","id":1069637,"title":"","content":"Another way to look at it is the role of Consilia at the table in the game. Consilia are another source of mysteries - specifically magical whodunnits. Contrast that with Vampire where the politics are about power, intrigue, clashing interests, and favors. Certainly, this isn't a hard and fast distinction. Just an observation of how the supernatural quasi governments support their respective games' themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T15:54:23-07:00","id":1069679,"title":"","content":"The core difference between the two is that the Free Council believe in each Mage's vote and the Silver Ladder believe that the wisest and most experienced should be trusted with the responsibility of decisions.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are strengths and weaknesses to each when applied to Mages. But that's basically what they disagree on when it comes to practical politics. When it comes to policy on Sleepers and dealing with agents of The Lie they are good buddies. So yeah they argue constantly but when it comes to actual situations, they tend to agree vociferously in my experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:10:10-07:00","id":1069687,"title":"","content":"I think the key problem is that this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069574#post1069574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you decide to stop paying taxes, your government will put you into jail, and you may not decide to stop being a citizen and still live there.<br /> Consilium will tax you and expect you to obey it's law...but it's up to you if you want to subscribe. You join wanting benefits, and in exchange you are expected to follow Consiliums guidance.</div> </div> </div> </div>... is way too modern in its mode of thought.<br /> <br /> Not all governments work that way or have worked that way. The Consilium is not a <i>modern </i>government. It's an ancient thing; perhaps as old as agriculture. The Assembly is descended from this system, in the same way modern parliaments are ultimately descended from things and folkmoots.<br /> <br /> The Consilium is more like a... Well, like a folkmoot, really; you even have dueling (holmgang) as a means of dispute resolution. These sorts of gatherings were more democratic than Consilia are, but ultimately the principle is the same: If you're a part of a community, you attend the folkmoots, have a say in the law, and, if you have a dispute with a fellow, the moot resolves it through a legal channel.<br /> <br /> If you're not part of that community, though, you're an outlaw. That means that the law doesn't bind you, but nor does it protect you, and others are free to do to you as they see fit.<br /> <br /> That's how most small communities have had their law function pretty much since forever. That's how governments of that nature have functioned, often with a chieftain or king being responsible for organizing and holding (and, at times, enforcing) the law.<br /> <br /> Consilia are similar. They exist as a dispute resolution mechanism for members but largely ignore outsiders. They will get involved for certain crimes and offenses - letting a murderer wander free is bad form - but otherwise they don't really care to get involved.<br /> <br /> Hence, I don't really see why a Consilia isn't a government. It's just not a modern one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:18:42-07:00","id":1069696,"title":"","content":"But the thing about Silver Ladder is that they believe each Mage is a part of Awakened Nation - even if Mage in question disagrees. Which means they have rights and can't be abused like dogs, simply because they are Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:22:24-07:00","id":1069699,"title":"","content":"Consilium aren't that old. The Neolithic was the age where agriculture blew up, we've seen what it's like there.<br /> <br /> The consilium of the Silver Ladder isn't so much of a government as a theocracy. They have an ideal, want you to live by it and believe it's right, but they do not rule over you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-28-2017, 07:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:32:00-07:00","id":1069705,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I always liked comparing them to organised religion - to uphold membership you are expected to follow certain rules, you get certain benefits in exchange, can get thrown out by a higher authority if you do something particularly nasty, and there are certain values they are expected to go out and enforce even on unwilling people - or to protect them from things they think deserve being protected on, no matter if you subscribe or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T16:36:22-07:00","id":1069709,"title":"","content":"Yeah I suppose theo<i>cracy</i> is the wrong term, it suggests some sort of 'veiled in religion' totalitarianism But they are the priests and 'wise people' of the Diamond.<br /> <br /> And obviously individuals and individual examples can differ as much as you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-28-2017, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T17:32:58-07:00","id":1069735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069699#post1069699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consilium aren't that old. The Neolithic was the age where agriculture blew up, we've seen what it's like there.<br /> <br /> The consilium of the Silver Ladder isn't so much of a government as a theocracy. They have an ideal, want you to live by it and believe it's right, but they do not rule over you.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Consilium was built by the Silver Ladder, but it's a grouping of all Mages in a region. What you're describing is the Ladder itself as an Order. The Consilium has <i>laws</i>, and it enforces them, many whether you agree with them or not. Truck with the Abyss? Steal souls? The Sentinels are going to come for you if word reaches the Hierarch's ear, whether you're a member or not.<br /> <br /> Don't confuse the Consilium's conflict resolution mechanisms with its actual effecting of law, because it does both.<br /> <br /> Also, agriculture appears at different times in different places but fair enough. At the very least, Consilia are several thousand years old as a system, which would make them as old as folkmoots, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T18:18:16-07:00","id":1069756,"title":"","content":"Consilium (unless something is really wrong with it) wont force you into paying a tribute of Mana and research notes if you refuse to participate in it. It won't send Sentinels to invade your Sanctum, dispel your shields, drag you in front Hierarch, and then spoon feed him the Mana you &quot;owned him&quot; for &quot;right to exist in this region&quot;. It will, however, pester you about not returning a borrowed book, and it might refuse to let you use community resources if you are in bad standing, because you didn't pay the &quot;Mana Tax&quot;. <br /> But it won't require you to wear a funny hat if you are not a subscriber, and it probably also won't negotiate safety of your Mysteries with other Mages. Or of your territory, when it comes to Seers.<br /> <br /> Mages don't really need a government; if they don't like how things are, they can literally just stop coming and tell you to stop pestering them. And then you are going to do...what? Magically break their legs and tell them to make sure they have protection money ready tomorrow, because what a cute Mystery you have here, would be a tragedy if someone got their hands on her? They are more like secret societies aimed towards progressing goals of their members; and these goals tend to be &quot;leave me alone, let me Mystery in peace, and maybe lend me a book or two when I need it, yeah sure I will cast a spell for you from time to time whatever&quot;<br /> <br /> It will, however, slap you on the hand if you harm their members, because that's their duty. Soul Stealing and Abyss are a special case; Diamond seem to consider health of soul their mission, kinda like how Catholic Church will push for protection of unborn babies. <br /> <br /> Silver Ladder - dominated Consilia will, at their best, protect even Apostates, Free Councilors, Nameless Orders, Sleepwalkers and Sleepers from Banishers, Seers and other threats simply because they consider it to be inborn right of all Awakened and potentially-Awakened. At their worst, they are invaders who will tell you how to live your life and act like you subscribe to their ideology, because they believe that as a member of Awakened Nation, you need to act in certain way. They are the priest who invades your bedroom and tells you what you can or cannot do in it, and will not care about the fact that you don't follow his religion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T18:54:59-07:00","id":1069770,"title":"","content":"... Why do you assume any of that stuff is necessary for something to be a government? A government doesn't need to tax people to be a government; merely to make and enforce laws. There are whole sections of the world and long stretches of history with few, if any, direct taxes enforced by governments. That's the way small communities have operated for a very, very long time. Small, direct democracies don't actually need much infrastructure and, hence, much taxation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:11:15-07:00","id":1069776,"title":"","content":"Do you consider your local RPG club a government? Or the forum moderation? Or organised religion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:13:32-07:00","id":1069779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069770#post1069770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Why do you assume any of that stuff is necessary for something to be a government? A government doesn't need to tax people to be a government; merely to make and enforce laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's because that definition is so broad it could encompass this very forum, which makes and enforces rules for the forum's community but can't seriously be considered a government. And a number of other things, from high school and fraternities to public swimming pools and baseball games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:40:09-07:00","id":1069797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069776#post1069776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you consider your local RPG club a government? Or the forum moderation? Or organised religion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> None of those entities use force to enforce their judicial edicts (in the modern norm for organized religions anyway). Conciliums do. They don't tax you for existing in a territory normally, but you are expected to obey their laws in their territory regardless of whether you've opted in or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:50:39-07:00","id":1069800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069797#post1069797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of those entities use force to enforce their judicial edicts (in the modern norm for organized religions anyway). Conciliums do.</div> </div> </div> </div>They might not, actually. Their harshest punishment might be banishment or shunning, like being banned from a forum or ecommunicated from a religion or kicked out of a social group. Nothing says a consilium is only a consilium when force is a possible punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T19:51:30-07:00","id":1069801,"title":"","content":"edit: nevermind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-28-2017, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-28T20:50:56-07:00","id":1069841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069779#post1069779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's because that definition is so broad it could encompass this very forum, which makes and enforces rules for the forum's community but can't seriously be considered a government. And a number of other things, from high school and fraternities to public swimming pools and baseball games.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a broad definition. It's a broad definition because &quot;government&quot; is a term that has applied to everything from an absolute tyranny to pure democracy; from societies where ideas of currency do not even exist, to the economies of the developed world today. We even have terms like &quot;student government&quot;. It is a <i>broad</i> term.<br /> <br /> We tend to only refer to the term &quot;government&quot; in general instances when talking about a society in the larger sense but that's an arbitrary limitation we put upon the word, which is why I can say...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1069776#post1069776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you consider your local RPG club a government? Or the forum moderation? Or organised religion?</div> </div> </div> </div>These all probably fit the broadest definition of a government. RPG clubs, moderators, and organized religions can all create rules and generally exclude people from their groups if they refuse to obey them. Today, some organized religions <i>are</i> governments; the Pope is the head of a nation-state, with the power to set fiscal policy for banks, imprison people, and hire mercenaries; all things he has done and continues to do. Saudi Arabia outright runs on religious law.<br /> <br /> Taxation is not a necessity for government and never has been. It is simply a descriptor of how a society is controlled and regulated (i.e. governed). That societies with chieftains and reeves and mayors have existed without any form of direct taxation across the centuries is proof enough that this is the case. Many communes have no sense of private property, and hence no taxation, yet still have governments in the form of direct democracy or elected representatives.<br /> <br /> Consilia make and produce laws and enforce them within their jurisdiction. Some might only apply to members but others apply with force and vigor to all within the territory. The Boston Consilium is noted as banishing any non-members who make waves, and... Being unkind to those who refuse to take the ban with good grace. They have elected officials who make, decide on, and adjudicate that law. If you don't consider it a government because they don't demand a tithe, I don't know what to tell you.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T06:34:32-07:00","id":1070017,"title":"","content":"Ok, if you are using such definition, I'm going to agree that rulebook friendly Consilium is basically a secret society self government with voluntary membership that ignores rules and laws of sleeper society, and self-governs in order to provide it's members with benefits, safety and will expect signed up parties to follow the rules they agreed to following by being a member (even if they had no say in estabilishing these rules). The &quot;ignore sleeper society rules&quot; thing means that Consilium might be like a very hardcore Research Club that might punch you for not bringing back a book.I mean, I can understand what you are aiming at, because a thesis of one of my papers is basically that certain organized crime societies have risen up as a competition government in response for dissatisfaction with their proper rulers.<br /> <br /> But, however, &quot;healthy&quot; Consilium shouldn't be much more than a glorified Hobbyist Club. It shouldn't exist to progress political agenda of hierarch or councilors, and it shouldn't be interested in ruling the Mages instead of providing them with a safe space to research and occasionally complain at each other for stuff. And when you talk about &quot;Consilium as Government&quot;, I think that most people see a political body with it's own political interests that intends on ruling the Mages under it.<br /> Taxation was an example of something that Consilium can declare it members should do, but what it should not enforce on unwilling Mages that don't participate in the Magic Club.<br /> <br /> Anyway, everything I hear about Boston Consilium (excuse me, but my collection of 1st ED books is pathetic, and I don't intend to buy books from it now, and it really irritates me that it seems to be a default assumption that in order to play 2nd ED you are expected to possess most of the previous game) makes me feel that it's not really a good example &quot;default&quot; Consilium - it seems to be a dark twisted corrupted version of Consilium that exactly shows why it shouldn't end up being a government in the popular meaning of the word.<br /> <br /> <br /> My own Consilia tend to portray the opposite end of the spectrum - they are very uninvolved, caring only about it's members, and existing only for the specific purpose of helping Mages do their stuff in peace. They don't care if you are killing Sleepers with your research, or mutating animals, or torturing ghosts - it's not their business. As long as you don't destroy souls, as long as you don't hurt another member, you are free to do whatever you want. Consilium dosen't care. It has no right to judge your research and your Obsession. It exists specifically in order to allow free pursue of Obsessions.<br /> <br /> By the way, maybe we should split this conversation to another thread, because we stopped talking about Mutapan era looong time ago, and there are probably people who would want to talk about it but are intimidated by this argument or feel bad/rude about interrupting it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 03-29-2017, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T07:21:19-07:00","id":1070042,"title":"","content":"The Boston Consilium is a wreck. I love it as a setting for Mage but as a default Consilium it was a bad idea, I think. That said I do intend to use the Boston Consilium as a trip away for when I run my London Consilium game, so the players can investigate somewhere else (they'll learn about a Runewalk in Boston and go across to try and see what secrets they can discern from it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T11:49:29-07:00","id":1070215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1070017#post1070017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-words-</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like a lot of this discussion was caused by having different definitions of the word government, then. I'm glad that's sorted.<br /> <br /> On the topic of Consilia, I have a slightly different view of things. I agree that Consilia strive to be hands off, because Mages will flip the bird at anyone who tries to encroach on them too much, and that 90% of what a Consilium does is basically prevent pissing matches between local Awakened from turning into magical wars.<br /> <br /> It's that remaining 10% where I disagree and, even then, it's not by much. The number of laws beyond &quot;What not to do to your fellow Mages&quot; that a given Consilium has will generally be few and basically consist entirely of &quot;Don't engage in Left-Handed Practices or join the Seers&quot;. However, it's those laws where I believe the Consilium says that membership doesn't matter. Scelesti, Reapers, those that reveal the Mysteries to Sleepers, etc., aren't going to escape the Consilium's attentions.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Consilia are political. Not overtly, all that often - a Hierarch who just creates laws at odds with the ideas of the masses is going to get booted - but enough. A deacon in the high chair will give different rulings to a hierophant or epopt.<br /> <br /> If that doesn't sound all that different than your own system, then we're not really in disagreement at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1070017#post1070017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, maybe we should split this conversation to another thread, because we stopped talking about Mutapan era looong time ago, and there are probably people who would want to talk about it but are intimidated by this argument or feel bad/rude about interrupting it?</div> </div> </div> </div>We probably should, yeah. Hopefully the book will be out for the rest of us today.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T18:38:04-07:00","id":1070419,"title":"","content":"...man, this Mutapan thread sure is giving some awesome stuff about Mutapa..<br /> <br /> *ahem*<br /> <br /> The way I see it, the Consilium strives to handle things that-- if they <i>didn't</i> handle them,-- would result in the various Cabals getting together and lynching the locals. There a major Scelestus in the area causing all kinds of Abyssal problems? You better handle that, before it causes a problem and you're left with half the city on fire. The same with, say, Reapers or people being too blatant with the Mysteries.<br /> <br /> The basic <i>definition</i> of Left-Handed Practices is that they're things that the local body of mages doesn't approve of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T06:22:20-07:00","id":1070601,"title":"","content":"Something I've been wondering about is the apparent lack of Seers in the Mutapan Empire. I kinda wonder if it might not be because their concept of God is quite different.<br /> <br /> If I follow it right, their creator god Mwari isn't an omni-benevolent God, they created evil as well. Therefore the idea of serving God, or the Exarchs doesn't conceptually make much sense.<br /> <br /> You can see a sort of similarity in the Pelasgian beliefs where the Exarchs aren't the ultimate tyrant sorcerers but more naturally occuring flaws to be worked around.<br /> <br /> The modern Seers seem to conceptualise the Exarchs as tyrants actively oppressing the sleepers, and you either serve them or oppose them. It's a very manichean view, and I don't know that it would make sense outside that kind of conceptual worldview.<br /> <br /> I find it noteworthy that the Diadochi only appeared at the intersection between the Pelasgian followers of Alexander and the Karpani who seem to conceptualise the Exarchs as an evil quasi-deity. Makes me wonder how much of the entire Diamond vs. Seer war is essentially the product of the Awakened conceptualising the conflict in that manner.<br /> <br /> Just a few wild speculations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:13:36-07:00","id":1070647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1070601#post1070601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I've been wondering about is the apparent lack of Seers in the Mutapan Empire. I kinda wonder if it might not be because their concept of God is quite different.<br /> <br /> If I follow it right, their creator god Mwari isn't an omni-benevolent God, they created evil as well. Therefore the idea of serving God, or the Exarchs doesn't conceptually make much sense.<br /> <br /> You can see a sort of similarity in the Pelasgian beliefs where the Exarchs aren't the ultimate tyrant sorcerers but more naturally occuring flaws to be worked around.<br /> <br /> The modern Seers seem to conceptualise the Exarchs as tyrants actively oppressing the sleepers, and you either serve them or oppose them. It's a very manichean view, and I don't know that it would make sense outside that kind of conceptual worldview.<br /> <br /> I find it noteworthy that the Diadochi only appeared at the intersection between the Pelasgian followers of Alexander and the Karpani who seem to conceptualise the Exarchs as an evil quasi-deity. Makes me wonder how much of the entire Diamond vs. Seer war is essentially the product of the Awakened conceptualising the conflict in that manner.<br /> <br /> Just a few wild speculations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if it's just a matter of how Seer beliefs are transmitted versus Diamond ones. The Diamond started out as cross cultural interactions that met both in realspace and in the Astral. This allows Diamond Darshanas to transcend distance. The first Seer ministry came out of one of the Great Cults of Greece and started attaching itself to temporally powerful figures. They don't want to recruit like-minded mages via the Astral. They want to conquer them in realspace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:28:03-07:00","id":1070662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1067158-mutapan-empire?p=1070647#post1070647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it's just a matter of how Seer beliefs are transmitted versus Diamond ones. The Diamond started out as cross cultural interactions that met both in realspace and in the Astral. This allows Diamond Darshanas to transcend distance. The first Seer ministry came out of one of the Great Cults of Greece and started attaching itself to temporally powerful figures. They don't want to recruit like-minded mages via the Astral. They want to conquer them in realspace.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a legit point. The Seers do seem to have a real single point of origin that the Diamond don't have.<br /> <br /> Even the Diadochi don't really act like Seers. It seems more like they have their mage-centric imperial ambitions first and only then does that seem to attract the interest of the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> I believe that's closer to authorial intention than my speculation. I'm sure I remember Dave mentioning in passing that the Seers are really the Exarchs taking a more active role in response to the formation of the Diamond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:36:58-07:00","id":1076285,"title":"","content":"Something I uncover when making char sheet for Shona with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24\" data-vbnamecard=\"24\">Mr Gone</a> - there is missing name for Gnosis equivalent. I know we cannot have everything translated, but with having other name for Mana ( as Simba ) and having Gnosis left on sheet it seems... weird.`","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}